  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1223 AM MDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nThe Monsoon high will weaken further Tuesday and the upper level\nridge axis will remain oriented west to east across the region. A\nbackdoor front will bring added forcing and moisture to the\ncentral mountain chain Tuesday, leading to an uptick in convection\nthat will spread into the adjacent eastern highlands during the\nlate afternoon hours. Meanwhile across western NM, a moderate to\nmajor heat risk will persist across the lower elevations and an \nadvisory may be required for the middle RGV and Northwest Plateau.\nThe Monsoon high is forecast to lift north to over NV/UT and\nstrengthen from Wed into the weekend, taking the edge off of the\nheat across NM but with no significant moisture infusion. Daily\nrounds of convection are forecast, but with lower coverage and\nlower PWATs than one would normally expect for early August.",
